{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Kaplan&limit=10&title=Monsoon","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Monsoon ","subTitle":"the Indian Ocean and the future of American power "},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Kaplan, Robert D.,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1952-"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York "}}],"dateIssued":[{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2010"},"c2010"],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Random House"},"edition":"1st ed."},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"366 p. ; 25 cm."},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"map"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"In \"Monsoon,\" a pivotal examination of the Indian Ocean region and the countries known as \"Monsoon Asia,\" bestselling author Robert D. Kaplan deftly shows how crucial this dynamic area has become to American power in the twenty-first century. Kaplan also offers riveting insights into the economic and naval strategies of China and India and how they will affect U.S. interests, while also providing an on-the-ground perspective on the more volatile countries in the region."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Preface : The Rimland of Eurasia -- China expands vertically, India horizontally -- Oman is everywhere -- Curzon's frontiers -- \"Lands of India\" -- Baluchistan and Sindh -- The troubled rise of Gujarat -- The view from Delhi -- Bangladesh : the existential challenge -- Kolkata : the next global city -- Of strategy and beauty -- Sri Lanka : the new geopolitics -- Burma : where India and China collide -- Indonesia's tropical Islam -- The heart of maritime Asia -- China's two-ocean strategy? -- Unity and anarchy -- Zanzibar : the last frontier."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"by Robert D. Kaplan."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":[{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"i------"},{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}]},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":["United States","Indian Ocean Region"],"topic":"Foreign relations"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":["Indian Ocean Region","United States"],"topic":"Foreign relations"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"Indian Ocean Region","topic":"Strategic aspects"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"National security","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"National security","geographic":"Indian Ocean Region"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"DS341.3.U6 K374 2010"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"327.73018 K17m"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"327.730182/4"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781400067466 (alk. paper)"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^2009049752"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"477270897"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990123182750203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"DS341.3.U6 K374 2010"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"DS341.3.U6 K374 2010"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":["Lamont","Widener"]},"originalDocument":"https://s3.am